course: dictionary
lesson: 9796
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Suspension has four, so the sentence around it tells you which one you need. «A suspension bridge hangs its road from huge cables slung over tall towers.» Here suspension is part of a bridge's name, and it describes how the road is held up by cables.
explain: «Then his new secondary school asked about the suspension, because it was on his record.» A school record holds serious incidents, so here suspension means a pupil being kept away from school for a time as a punishment. The word "record" is the clue.
explain: In science, a suspension is a liquid with tiny bits of a solid floating in it, like muddy water. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Does "the mud is floating in the water" still make sense? Yes, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Suspension can mean a punishment that keeps a pupil away from school for a time.
fact: Suspension can also mean a pause or stop to something for a time, as in «suspension of play».
fact: A car's suspension is the springs and parts that make the ride smooth over bumps.
fact: A suspension bridge hangs its road from steel cables held up by tall towers.
fact: In science, a suspension has tiny bits of solid floating in a liquid, and they do not dissolve.
exercise: «A suspension bridge usually has 2 tall towers.» What holds up the road of a suspension bridge? | Wooden posts in the river | Balloons full of air | Blocks of ice | *Steel cables held up by tall towers
exercise: «Serious incidents like suspensions are written on a pupil's school record.» What does suspension mean here? | *Being kept away from school for a time as a punishment | A pause in a game | Springs that make a car ride smooth | A liquid with bits floating in it
exercise: Which mixture is a suspension? | Clear apple juice | Salt fully dissolved in water | Air in a balloon | *Sand floating in water that does not dissolve
test: The referee called a suspension of play while the rain fell. What does suspension mean here? | A liquid spilled on the grass | A bridge over the pitch | *A pause or stop to the game for a time | A punishment for a player
test: A bumpy road makes a car bounce, but a good suspension keeps the ride smooth. What is the suspension? | A wheel with a flat tyre | *The springs and parts that make the ride smooth over bumps | The engine that makes the car go | The seats inside the car
exam: Which sentence uses suspension to mean a liquid with tiny solid bits floating in it? | The car's suspension made the ride smooth | *Shake the bottle, because the suspension must be mixed before you pour | The suspension bridge crossed the wide river | The pupil's suspension was written on his record
